# AP Core Privacy Policy

Last updated: September 12, 2026

AP Core ("the app") is made by Michael LaBarbera ("we"). This policy explains what the app collects, why, and what you can do about it.

## What we collect

**Account.** When you sign in with Apple, Google, or an email code, we store your email address so you can sign in again. If you use Apple's Hide My Email, we only receive the relay address Apple gives us.

**Study data.** Your enrolled courses, progress, practice answers, notes, mistake log, and planner items are stored on your device. Free-response answers you ask the AI grader to score are sent to our server for grading and are not stored there.

**Purchases.** If you subscribe or buy an exam pass, Apple handles payment. We receive only a receipt that tells the app what you own. We never see your card details.

**Usage analytics.** We record which screens and features are used, tagged with a random identifier created when the app is installed. This is not linked to your name or email. You can turn it off in Profile under "Share anonymous usage stats".

**Advertising.** The free tier shows ads through Google AdMob, configured for non-personalized ads. Google may collect device information to serve and measure those ads; see Google's privacy policy at https://policies.google.com/privacy. Premium removes ads.

**Notifications.** If you allow notifications, reminder times are stored on your device only.

## What we don't do

We do not sell your data. We do not track you across other companies' apps or websites. We do not collect location, contacts, photos, or precise device identifiers.

## Where data goes

Study content is generated and served through Supabase (hosted database and functions) and Google's Gemini API. Prompts sent to Gemini contain course and question text, and, for the AI grader, the answer you typed. They do not contain your name or email.

## Your choices

- **Delete your account** in the app: Profile, Delete Account. This deletes your account and removes all app data from your phone.
- **Sign out** removes all app data from your phone.
- **Turn off analytics** in Profile.
- **Manage subscriptions** in your Apple ID settings.

## Children

AP Core is for high school students preparing for AP exams and is rated for ages 13 and up. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.

